This repository is focused around building an effort to clean up trash in neighborhoods/zones.
Users will be able to create a new account with their existing Google, Apple or Facebook accounts.
Users will be presented with zones where there is a current need for someone to take a walk with a trash bag, PPE, and maybe a good ol' stick with a nail in the end and clean up.
->It won't be suggested that users try to clean up anything more than what can fit in a trash bag.
->If a user gets done cleaning up trash, and it's still trashy, they can report it that way.
Users will be presented with zones around their current location where they can report how much trash is lying around.
->Think, I'm walking to work and it's hella gross on Broad street because the Phillies won so I pull up the app, click the zone I'm in and click a 'trash on the ground' icon.
->Alternatively, I'm walking to work and it looks clean, so I open the app and click a green check mark, or maybe there is a 'light trash' icon because there's some but it's not gross.
Users will have the ability to share their efforts via Instagram/Facebook/Twitter
Users will get points for the amount of time spent in an area, for the number of times they sign up, for cleaning streaks or reporting streaks.

Beyond that, I don't really want to get too crazy. 
This is an opportunity to work with GPS location, a map, drawing elements/creating a ui on/over the map.
